body:
A `Regex` can't be `const`, but you can make it `static` using a static cell such as  `std::sync::OnceLock`.

You can do this:
```rust
fn root_regex() -> &'static Regex {
    static ROOT_REGEX: OnceLock<Regex> = OnceLock::new();

    ROOT_REGEX.get_or_init(|| {
        Regex::new(r"^/").unwrap()
    })
}

fn root_regex_final() -> &'static Regex {
    static ROOT_REGEX_FINAL: OnceLock<Regex> = OnceLock::new();

    ROOT_REGEX_FINAL.get_or_init(|| {
        Regex::new(r"^root/?").unwrap()
    })
}
```

This way, the regex will be initialized just once and calling `root_regex()` will give you the same ref every time. The static `OnceLock`s are defined inside functions to hide them from the rest of the module.

